# Optional DDL discovery uses existing authenticated settings; Requests remains default and owns archive transfers.
# Mylar3 – copy to stack.env. Set PUID/PGID to match host if using bind-mounted comics/downloads.
# Docs: https://docs.linuxserver.io/images/docker-mylar3

# Optional: user/group for file ownership (default 1000)
# PUID=1000
# PGID=1000

# TZ/locale: use shared.env (see documents/SHARED-RESOURCES.md)

# Unified media tree (host → /data). Use /data/comics for the library.
MYLAR3_MEDIA_PATH=/path/to/media

# Pack verification requires the matching maintenance worker; enable both in their settings.
# Activity settings live in the UI; back up workflow.sqlite with the config volume.
# Published image; pin a sha-<commit> tag or digest for reproducible redeployments.
MYLAR3_IMAGE=ghcr.io/bolens/homelab-mylar3:latest

# ComicTagger backend is selected in Metadata Tagging settings; Legacy is default.
# Modern is an experimental opt-in for CBZ ComicRack metadata; conversion stays with the normalizer.
# Shared normalizer coordination uses media-writer inside the existing config volume.
# Configure the matching worker override separately; no additional Mylar mount is needed.

# Converted ComicInfo follow-up uses mylar.tag_converted in the private normalizer config.
# Enable only after matching Mylar deployment and shared writer coordination; see README.
